    "created_at": "2022-06-07T09:01:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-07T09:01:24Z",
    "body": "That could work as well, to some extent this depends on whether we expect web developers to branch on the exception type. If we don't, using the generic exception is preferred (that's `TypeError` to be clear).\r\n\r\nI don't think we'd expect web developers to branch here. At least not based on this, but I could be mistaken. It seems to me that if the OS limit needs to be exposed there are better ways to do that, e.g., through a static getter.",
